{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/984941-seeing-through-the-eyes-of-a-mage","id":984941,"title":"Seeing through the eyes of a mage","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-10T10:42:08-07:00","id":984941,"title":"Seeing through the eyes of a mage","content":"Anyone else wonder what it's like just to see what a mage sees when they look at things? For instance take a newly awakened mage with one dot in correspondence, think about it, they effectively have 360* night vision without even considering other spheres. An entropy 1 mage can see fate, and the weaknesses in objects tsukihime/garden of sinners style. A life 1 mage could see all the inner workings of any living organism. a mind 1 mage can read emotions and what a person is currently thinking about. etc.<br /> <br /> just imagine how much different a persons world view would be if they could see magical potential in everything with prime 1. Or what new breakthroughs a scientist(non-magical) could make with just forces or matter 1. It's the reason I let players Use mage sensing with perception + awareness rather than arete, just seeing things for the first time after the awakening should be an incomparable and breathtaking experience.<br /> <br /> (all except time 1. While rare always knowing what time it is is possible for mundane people and as a power it's next to useless. Not to mention seeing the future is sensory, so don't understand why it's time 2)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6383,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","user":"Prometheas","date":". 10-10-2016, 01:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T11:36:23-07:00","id":984969,"title":"","content":"I also HR that we skip the arete roll for sensory magick and go directly to the roll that determines what they get out of their mage sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T11:47:13-07:00","id":984978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/984941-seeing-through-the-eyes-of-a-mage#post984941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(all except time 1. While rare always knowing what time it is is possible for mundane people and as a power it's next to useless. Not to mention seeing the future is sensory, so don't understand why it's time 2)</div> </div> </div> </div>Time 1 is the single most underrated sphere stat in the game. Time 1 doesn't just let you know what time it is, it gives you Perfect Time Sense, you can perfectly intuit how long things take and how much time you need to do things. You know exactly when you need to get things done before the bus leaves and never miss a bus. You know exactly how much time has passed since you arrived somewhere, so no disorientation for you. You know exactly what time it is no matter where or when you are. Accidental time travel? No reading newspapers to determine the date for you, that's already covered. Captured and taken hostage for hours on end? You know exactly how long they've kept you, how long you've been travelling and how long you've been stationary, information you might need when considering an escape strategy. How about doing complicated procedures? With perfect Time Sense, you can do about 10 or so at once staggered from one another and never get a single one out of sync.<br /> <br /> With enough practice, you know exactly how long it takes to get from one place to another on various methods, and can plan your day down to the millisecond with perfect precision. No moment is wasted, and nothing is left to chance. Combined with Entropy 1, this becomes insane! You basically become Batman levels of prepared.<br /> <br /> Mixed with other spheres, you can make on going effects stop at precisely the time you intend them to, no more &quot;stop at the end of a scene, or the day&quot; now it's &quot;Stop precisely at 3pm tomorrow&quot; or &quot;Stop after exactly 15 hours&quot;. You can make Corr. gates which change location at specific times of day, Force bound temperatures that fluctuate between hot and cold depending on whether it's day or night, Spirit gates which only open for one hour at midnight. Guns that morph into gloves during the day... Any effect that you want to have multiple steps to it based on time delays needs Time 1 to pull of. Plus, with Time 1 you can sense all the temporal elements of other mage's effects. So if you come across these Time sensitive gates or items, you may not know what will happen, but you'll certainly know when it will.<br /> <br /> Also, what is the one sphere that when used, no matter how well you've planned, how much you've achieved, how many things you've accomplished, all of that can be rendered moot simply by making it all not happen? Time! What's the one point sphere that actually clues you in to when this kind of stuff is happening? Time 1! Think about it. You're in a battle and everything you throw at them, they seem to be ready for it. Any ambush, any surprise, any secret, they can react to it without a moment's hesitation. The truth is that they're using Time magic to change things to happen their way, and there is no way you could possibly know about this without Time 1. Knowing that mages are messing around with the time stream is impossible without this sphere. You don't know people are spying on you from across time, that they keep undoing your work and sabotaging your attempts before you even get a chance to pull them out of the bag. Time 1 is the only thing that might clue you in to what's going on. Without that, you're pretty much sunk.<br /> <br /> Regarding Time 2, Future and Past sight can be really easily abused if you give the player a chance. They can use it to know almost everything about anything. They know exactly who committed what crimes, where things might have been stolen, where things were hidden, and what people might do if you let them do it. If this sphere was at the 1st rank, it would be even more ridiculous than it already is.<br /> <br /> Besides, Time 2 Future Sight is not exactly unlike Corr. 2 Scrying. Only one is temporal while the other is spatial, so it does make sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 10-10-2016, 04:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T14:29:12-07:00","id":985068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/984941-seeing-through-the-eyes-of-a-mage?p=984978#post984978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Time 1 is the single most underrated sphere stat in the game. Time 1 doesn't just let you know what time it is, it gives you Perfect Time Sense, you can perfectly intuit how long things take and how much time you need to do things. You know exactly when you need to get things done before the bus leaves and never miss a bus. You know exactly how much time has passed since you arrived somewhere, so no disorientation for you. You know exactly what time it is no matter where or when you are. Accidental time travel? No reading newspapers to determine the date for you, that's already covered. Captured and taken hostage for hours on end? You know exactly how long they've kept you, how long you've been travelling and how long you've been stationary, information you might need when considering an escape strategy. How about doing complicated procedures? With perfect Time Sense, you can do about 10 or so at once staggered from one another and never get a single one out of sync.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could also technically do most of that by having a watch or increasing your intelligence to 5/giving yourself multiple mental actions with mind 1. Heck. With matter 1 and a watch, you'd just have to sense when the numbers on your watch change to know what time it is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/984941-seeing-through-the-eyes-of-a-mage?p=984978#post984978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With enough practice, you know exactly how long it takes to get from one place to another on various methods, and can plan your day down to the millisecond with perfect precision. No moment is wasted, and nothing is left to chance. Combined with Entropy 1, this becomes insane! You basically become Batman levels of prepared.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also doable with entropy and high int alone.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/984941-seeing-through-the-eyes-of-a-mage?p=984978#post984978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mixed with other spheres, you can make on going effects stop at precisely the time you intend them to, no more &quot;stop at the end of a scene, or the day&quot; now it's &quot;Stop precisely at 3pm tomorrow&quot; or &quot;Stop after exactly 15 hours&quot;. You can make Corr. gates which change location at specific times of day, Force bound temperatures that fluctuate between hot and cold depending on whether it's day or night, Spirit gates which only open for one hour at midnight. Guns that morph into gloves during the day... Any effect that you want to have multiple steps to it based on time delays needs Time 1 to pull of. Plus, with Time 1 you can sense all the temporal elements of other mage's effects. So if you come across these Time sensitive gates or items, you may not know what will happen, but you'll certainly know when it will.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do believe it is a poor sphere effect that requires other spheres to be effective.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/984941-seeing-through-the-eyes-of-a-mage?p=984978#post984978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, what is the one sphere that when used, no matter how well you've planned, how much you've achieved, how many things you've accomplished, all of that can be rendered moot simply by making it all not happen? Time! What's the one point sphere that actually clues you in to when this kind of stuff is happening? Time 1! Think about it. You're in a battle and everything you throw at them, they seem to be ready for it. Any ambush, any surprise, any secret, they can react to it without a moment's hesitation. The truth is that they're using Time magic to change things to happen their way, and there is no way you could possibly know about this without Time 1. Knowing that mages are messing around with the time stream is impossible without this sphere. You don't know people are spying on you from across time, that they keep undoing your work and sabotaging your attempts before you even get a chance to pull them out of the bag. Time 1 is the only thing that might clue you in to what's going on. Without that, you're pretty much sunk.</div> </div> </div> </div>All spheres are able to sense when their influence is used or effected, that'd be a horrible sphere that didn't. Also even without time 1, you could just draw out the battle until your opponent exploded from paradox. If said person is using so much time, entropy, spirit, etc. magic that you can't do anything, they're using enough vulgar effects that it doesn't matter anyway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/984941-seeing-through-the-eyes-of-a-mage?p=984978#post984978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding Time 2, Future and Past sight can be really easily abused if you give the player a chance. They can use it to know almost everything about anything. They know exactly who committed what crimes, where things might have been stolen, where things were hidden, and what people might do if you let them do it. If this sphere was at the 1st rank, it would be even more ridiculous than it already is.<br /> <br /> Besides, Time 2 Future Sight is not exactly unlike Corr. 2 Scrying. Only one is temporal while the other is spatial, so it does make sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>And when aren't mage powers abused? Isn't that sort of the point? I do disagree with correspondence 2 as well, but its first level power is still exceedingly useful alone(night-vision, 360* perception, awareness of things that are obstructed from view(like on the other side of a wall), etc.).<br /> <br /> That's the problem I have with time 1, it's effect either requires other spheres to be useful, can be done without magic, or is only useful under such niche circumstances that it would rarely come up. Every other sphere 1(be it reading minds, seeing an enemy's weaknesses, perfect diagnosis/autopsy, sensing magic, hearing Radio Transmissions, etc.) are useful for many, many things in both magical and mundane life, can be useful on their own, and are rarely is there a situation where they aren't useful.<br /> <br /> This may simply be a case where we'll agree to disagree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T16:40:10-07:00","id":985122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/984941-seeing-through-the-eyes-of-a-mage?p=985068#post985068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This may simply be a case where we'll agree to disagree.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, that's boring.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/984941-seeing-through-the-eyes-of-a-mage?p=985068#post985068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You could also technically do most of that by having a watch or increasing your intelligence to 5/giving yourself multiple mental actions with mind 1. Heck. With matter 1 and a watch, you'd just have to sense when the numbers on your watch change to know what time it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because having a watch means you're never late? There is a huge difference between being able to know the time and actually feeling time. Your argument can be used on pretty much any sphere to demonstrate a lack of use.<br /> <br /> Corr 1? You could just do that with Mind 1 and high Perception! Heck, you can do this with cameras and a computer these days!<br /> Entropy 1? You could just use maths and common sense...<br /> Forces 1? Thermometer, Barometer, Light meter, Sound meter, Ampmeter, Geiger counter... Mundane world's got you covered.<br /> Life 1? All you need is some Biology and a keen eye.<br /> Matter 1? Science is literally all you need for these.<br /> Mind 1? You could just use empathy and basic psychology!<br /> Prime 1? Get yourself a periapt for the Quint, invest in awareness, and who cares?<br /> Spirit 1? Cosmology and Occult, and you're golden.<br /> <br /> Yeah, see how dismissive that comes across as?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/984941-seeing-through-the-eyes-of-a-mage?p=985068#post985068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also doable with entropy and high int alone.</div> </div> </div> </div>So 1 Time alone is equal to 1 Entropy + 5 Int, and you're trying to tell me Time 1 is not as good as Entropy 1? It means you don't need that the expensive 5 Int to do that...<br /> <br /> Also, your internal Mind clock has no guarantee of being correct if you've been knocked out. Time sense, on the other hand, will always be correct.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/984941-seeing-through-the-eyes-of-a-mage?p=985068#post985068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do believe it is a poor sphere effect that requires other spheres to be effective.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a hell of a lot more versatile than Prime 1, which is basically the power to have extra quintessence and see magic. How often has Prime 1 really been all that necessary for other sphere effects? Same goes for Spirit 1. You can't even touch spirits until Spirit 2, so why the heck is Spirit 1 going to be used for spirit targeting multisphere effects.<br /> <br /> Also. Consider this. If you had perfect timing, is it not inconceivable that certain rolls would be much easier to perform? Dexterity rolls perhaps? Perhaps turning on Time 1 could make your timing so good that all Dex rolls can have a reduction in difficulty depending on successes rolled. That makes it easier to dodge, easier to hit, easier to aim, and basically easier to combat in general. How's that?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/984941-seeing-through-the-eyes-of-a-mage?p=985068#post985068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> All spheres are able to sense when their influence is used or effected, that'd be a horrible sphere that didn't. Also even without time 1, you could just draw out the battle until your opponent exploded from paradox. If said person is using so much time, entropy, spirit, etc. magic that you can't do anything, they're using enough vulgar effects that it doesn't matter anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Two words: Time Marauders.<br /> <br /> Also yeah, completely ignore the bit about people scrying on you across time...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/984941-seeing-through-the-eyes-of-a-mage?p=985068#post985068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And when aren't mage powers abused? Isn't that sort of the point? I do disagree with correspondence 2 as well, but its first level power is still exceedingly useful alone(night-vision, 360* perception, awareness of things that are obstructed from view(like on the other side of a wall), etc.).</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't actually get &quot;nigh-vision 360 perception&quot; as you put it. You'd need Forces for the night vision part. All you get is a layout of the room. Without matter you can't see inside things, so no looking inside desks or drawers, you only see the big block of space the cupboard takes up, without life you can't see people or living things, so it's not much of a recon, and without boosting your int up with Mind, you may not even be able to handle all the information at once and still see things mundanely. So yeah, lots of drawbacks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/984941-seeing-through-the-eyes-of-a-mage?p=985068#post985068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the problem I have with time 1, it's effect either requires other spheres to be useful, can be done without magic, or is only useful under such niche circumstances that it would rarely come up. Every other sphere 1(be it reading minds, seeing an enemy's weaknesses, perfect diagnosis/autopsy, sensing magic, hearing Radio Transmissions, etc.) are useful for many, many things in both magical and mundane life, can be useful on their own, and are rarely is there a situation where they aren't useful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Forces 1 can also be done mundanely without too much trouble, just know Technology. Regarding Niche use, the same can be said for Spirit 1, if a campaign ain't involving the spirit world, it's not really relevant at all. Similarly Prime 1 is about as niche as you can get when it comes to actual effects.<br /> <br /> Also, you seemed to have biged up a few of the first level sphere's purview in order to make your point. Mind 1 cannot read minds, you get emotions at best. Entropy 1 cannot see &quot;The enemy's weakness&quot; without Life 1 if it's physical, or Matter 1 if it's material. Life 1 is only a perfect diagnosis if you have Medicine, and Life 1 can't be used for autopsy because a corpse is not a life pattern, it's a matter pattern.<br /> <br /> Again, sensing magic can be done with awareness and the relevant spheres involved, so not exactly unique to Prime 1, and hearing Radio waves only requires a Radio... That's kinda what they're built to do...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T18:16:17-07:00","id":985175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/984941-seeing-through-the-eyes-of-a-mage?p=985068#post985068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All spheres are able to sense when their influence is used or effected, that'd be a horrible sphere that didn't. Also even without time 1, you could just draw out the battle until your opponent exploded from paradox. If said person is using so much time, entropy, spirit, etc. magic that you can't do anything, they're using enough vulgar effects that it doesn't matter anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Paradox is not insurmountable.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T20:03:12-07:00","id":985230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/984941-seeing-through-the-eyes-of-a-mage?p=985122#post985122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Nah, that's boring.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Well...Okay</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/984941-seeing-through-the-eyes-of-a-mage?p=985122#post985122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Because having a watch means you're never late? There is a huge difference between being able to know the time and actually feeling time. Your argument can be used on pretty much any sphere to demonstrate a lack of use.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Corr 1? You could just do that with Mind 1 and high Perception! Heck, you can do this with cameras and a computer these days!</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Entropy 1? You could just use maths and common sense...</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Forces 1? Thermometer, Barometer, Light meter, Sound meter, Ampmeter, Geiger counter... Mundane world's got you covered.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Life 1? All you need is some Biology and a keen eye.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Matter 1? Science is literally all you need for these.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Mind 1? You could just use empathy and basic psychology!</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Prime 1? Get yourself a periapt for the Quint, invest in awareness, and who cares?</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Spirit 1? Cosmology and Occult, and you're golden.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Yeah, see how dismissive that comes across as?</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">1.you can't carry a building with security cameras around with you, 2. That seems pretty hard, but Possible I guess with mind enhancements, 3. A lot of expensive tech you can't carry everywhere, 4. doesn't work for internal injuries, 5. Define science/you can't carry an electron microscope everywhere or use it efficiently in the field, 6. doesn't really give you the int boosts or multy actions, 7. I guess(you'd loose out on wonders though, but the argument was &quot;without other spheres&quot;. so you win), 8. I'm pretty sure that doesn't let you see and talk to spirits....</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/984941-seeing-through-the-eyes-of-a-mage?p=985122#post985122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">So 1 Time alone is equal to 1 Entropy + 5 Int, and you're trying to tell me Time 1 is not as good as Entropy 1? It means you don't need that the expensive 5 Int to do that...</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Also, your internal Mind clock has no guarantee of being correct if you've been knocked out. Time sense, on the other hand, will always be correct.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Int 5 is expensive, but you can also get it with mind 1. Also you didn't say time alone, you stated time 1 + entropy 1 for batmaning. Having Mind 1 + entropy 1 do the same thing And have other benifits from mind 1 doesn't help your case.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/984941-seeing-through-the-eyes-of-a-mage?p=985122#post985122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">It's a hell of a lot more versatile than Prime 1, which is basically the power to have extra quintessence and see magic. How often has Prime 1 really been all that necessary for other sphere effects? Same goes for Spirit 1. You can't even touch spirits until Spirit 2, so why the heck is Spirit 1 going to be used for spirit targeting multisphere effects.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> You don't need to touch a spirit to convince it to kill someone/do a task in exchange for a favor or chinimage. Prime 1 lets you sense all magical effects on a person/object/area and what effects an enemy are likely to use(sense resonance).</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/984941-seeing-through-the-eyes-of-a-mage?p=985122#post985122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Also. Consider this. If you had perfect timing, is it not inconceivable that certain rolls would be much easier to perform? Dexterity rolls perhaps? Perhaps turning on Time 1 could make your timing so good that all Dex rolls can have a reduction in difficulty depending on successes rolled. That makes it easier to dodge, easier to hit, easier to aim, and basically easier to combat in general. How's that?</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> I don't see how that'd effect dex rolls, wits rolls sure, but not dex.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/984941-seeing-through-the-eyes-of-a-mage?p=985122#post985122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Two words: Time Marauders.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Also yeah, completely ignore the bit about people scrying on you across time...</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">One word: quiet. Marauders aren't immune to paradox, it just makes their quiet bubble worse until it's incompatible with reality an they're sent to la-la land in the spirit world. It's not like a mage with time 1 can stop them either, you'll be resorting to the same tactic either way.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">How is a guy with time 1 going to stop someone scrying them. You might as well use prime 1 to sense &quot;there is some kind of detection magic on you, but you can't tell what kind&quot;.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/984941-seeing-through-the-eyes-of-a-mage?p=985122#post985122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">You don't actually get &quot;nigh-vision 360 perception&quot; as you put it. You'd need Forces for the night vision part. All you get is a layout of the room. Without matter you can't see inside things, so no looking inside desks or drawers, you only see the big block of space the cupboard takes up, without life you can't see people or living things, so it's not much of a recon, and without boosting your int up with Mind, you may not even be able to handle all the information at once and still see things mundanely. So yeah, lots of drawbacks.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">1. correspondence senses everything in your immediate area, matter or living. The only reason you'd need life is to tell if something is alive, a vampire, or an artificial construct, cor 1 will just flag it as &quot;Human shaped&quot;. Otherwise it would require matter to sense anything matter. Also said awareness is not tampered with by it being dark as its not &quot;sight&quot;.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/984941-seeing-through-the-eyes-of-a-mage?p=985122#post985122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Forces 1 can also be done mundanely without too much trouble, just know Technology. Regarding Niche use, the same can be said for Spirit 1, if a campaign ain't involving the spirit world, it's not really relevant at all. Similarly Prime 1 is about as niche as you can get when it comes to actual effects.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> 1. Really, with forces 1 you could see any EM frequency(x-ray vision), listing to any sound frequency(super hearing), detect heat sources(track living things), and do it without the fussy imaging of night vision goggles. nothing today can do all that. 2. You can also speak to the spirits and offer chinimage. Spirits are probably the most useful friend a mage character could ever have.(you can also read auras, but mind does that as well) 3. You can sense Any type of magic with prime(though you just sense it as &quot;a sphere you don't have&quot; if you don't have a 1 in that kind of magic), and you can sense resonance(letting you know what kind of magic the other party uses often).</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/984941-seeing-through-the-eyes-of-a-mage?p=985122#post985122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Also, you seemed to have biged up a few of the first level sphere's purview in order to make your point. Mind 1 cannot read minds, you get emotions at best. Entropy 1 cannot see &quot;The enemy's weakness&quot; without Life 1 if it's physical, or Matter 1 if it's material. Life 1 is only a perfect diagnosis if you have Medicine, and Life 1 can't be used for autopsy because a corpse is not a life pattern, it's a matter pattern.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Again, sensing magic can be done with awareness and the relevant spheres involved, so not exactly unique to Prime 1, and hearing Radio waves only requires a Radio... That's kinda what they're built to do...</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Mind 1 was a flub up, I read &quot;read surface thoughts&quot; and thought that actually meant thoughts(wow say that three times fast), but it does make you a human lie detector, lets you read emotions and detect impulses(probably means &quot;what the person is most focused on at the time&quot;, the writing is vague). Entropy 1 description says you just need entropy to spot weak points, nothing about matter or life. Life 1 depends on how fresh it is. If it's still warm or has been put on ice(preserved) then it's life. If it's been dead for a while or has been &quot;processed&quot;(like a cotton t-shirt) then it's matter.(so getting to the crime scene early is important.)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Awareness vs prime is a valid point. Though having forces 1 is like having multiple type of heavy and expensive measuring equipment built into you head, so it's definitely worth it. Anyone can and most likely do carry a watch though, so my mind remains unchanged. :P</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/984941-seeing-through-the-eyes-of-a-mage?p=985175#post985175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Paradox is not insurmountable.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're fighting a mage so powerful that they can ignore paradox, the mage with only sphere 1s is going to lose. It doesn't matter which sphere 1s he has, he'll lose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T03:48:31-07:00","id":985343,"title":"","content":"Mind 2 reads surface thoughts, mind 1 is just emotion.<br /> Similarly, Spirit 2 is required to speak the language of the spirits, spirit 1 just let's you see them.<br /> Prime 1 does not let you make wonders, depending on the system, wonders are locked away from you until either prime 2 it 3.<br /> <br /> Try not to compare their higher level counterparts when comparing 1st level spheres.<br /> <br /> Here's the thing, if you're determined for Time 1 to be rubbish, then of course every game you run is going to have Time 1 as rubbish. As a Storyteller, we have a duty to our players to fulfil the needs of their magic. If your player chooses to put points into Spirt, then you must allow interactions with the spirit world in your game. If they put it in Prime, then you need to put nodes in your game.<br /> <br /> To just decide Time is useless like you have is a disservice to players that play under you who are interested in Time. It's like saying &quot;well, I don't understand Entropy, so I'm not going let you do that&quot;<br /> <br /> Every sphere at every level has to have a function and a use, and if you reject this idea then your game is worse off for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 10-11-2016, 06:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T04:47:08-07:00","id":985351,"title":"","content":"There was a thought experiment similar to this regarding Mage the Awakening over on the rpg.net forums. It was a fascinating look at what a starting mage of each path could do essentially for free and how it would affect the way they approach the world.<br /> <br /> There are a few really big differences between Ascension and Awakening, though, and the biggest of them is Paradigm. Sure Correspondence mages can see 360 and Time mages have perfect timing, but what that looks like varies wildly from mage to mage. So the Thanatoic might feel the pull of the wheel, while the Hermetic has a small record keeping Angel only he can see, and the Etherite just uses a really good watch. It's the same power, and having it will affect them all, but not necessarily in the same way.<br /> <br /> <br /> Both a wraith's Lifesight and Superman's X-ray vision would be outstanding boons to a doctor, but they are going to have very different impacts on how she sees the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T15:17:08-07:00","id":985711,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/984941-seeing-through-the-eyes-of-a-mage?p=985343#post985343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mind 2 reads surface thoughts, mind 1 is just emotion.</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/984941-seeing-through-the-eyes-of-a-mage?p=985343#post985343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Similarly, Spirit 2 is required to speak the language of the spirits, spirit 1 just let's you see them.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Prime 1 does not let you make wonders, depending on the system, wonders are locked away from you until either prime 2 it 3.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Try not to compare their higher level counterparts when comparing 1st level spheres.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Here's the thing, if you're determined for Time 1 to be rubbish, then of course every game you run is going to have Time 1 as rubbish. As a Storyteller, we have a duty to our players to fulfill the needs of their magic. If your player chooses to put points into Spirit, then you must allow interactions with the spirit world in your game. If they put it in Prime, then you need to put nodes in your game.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">To just decide Time is useless like you have is a disservice to players that play under you who are interested in Time. It's like saying &quot;well, I don't understand Entropy, so I'm not going let you do that&quot;.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Every sphere at every level has to have a function and a use, and if you reject this idea then your game is worse off for it.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">1. Sure, but what exactly are &quot;impulses&quot; then. I'm not arguing with you about the thought thing, I just have no idea what the writer meant by &quot;Impulse&quot;. 2. Unless the spirit speaks a human language, like say a wraith or a spirit of a human concept(nature spirits not so much). They're all perceivable at spirit 1, you just can't translate and talk to every spirit. 3. Oops, derp. :P</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Also why would I force a player not to take time 1 for any reason or keep them from doing anything cool with it(not that I've had one. Any player I've had take time at the start bought time 2 for future sight or if they bought time 1 with experience they'd ignore it till time 2.). I've never really seen anyone even Try to come up with a cool use for it.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/984941-seeing-through-the-eyes-of-a-mage?p=985351#post985351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There was a thought experiment similar to this regarding Mage the Awakening over on the rpg.net forums. It was a fascinating look at what a starting mage of each path could do essentially for free and how it would affect the way they approach the world.<br /> <br /> There are a few really big differences between Ascension and Awakening, though, and the biggest of them is Paradigm. Sure Correspondence mages can see 360 and Time mages have perfect timing, but what that looks like varies wildly from mage to mage. So the Thanatoic might feel the pull of the wheel, while the Hermetic has a small record keeping Angel only he can see, and the Etherite just uses a really good watch. It's the same power, and having it will affect them all, but not necessarily in the same way.<br /> <br /> <br /> Both a wraith's Lifesight and Superman's X-ray vision would be outstanding boons to a doctor, but they are going to have very different impacts on how she sees the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>^this. My frequent players and I always try to imagine what it would be like to suddenly see the world so differently, especially through paradigm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T17:46:57-07:00","id":985815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/984941-seeing-through-the-eyes-of-a-mage?p=984978#post984978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Time 1 is the single most underrated sphere stat in the game. Time 1 doesn't just let you know what time it is, it gives you Perfect Time Sense, you can perfectly intuit how long things take and how much time you need to do things. You know exactly when you need to get things done before the bus leaves and never miss a bus. You know exactly how much time has passed since you arrived somewhere, so no disorientation for you. You know exactly what time it is no matter where or when you are. Accidental time travel? No reading newspapers to determine the date for you, that's already covered. Captured and taken hostage for hours on end? You know exactly how long they've kept you, how long you've been travelling and how long you've been stationary, information you might need when considering an escape strategy. How about doing complicated procedures? With perfect Time Sense, you can do about 10 or so at once staggered from one another and never get a single one out of sync.<br /> <br /> With enough practice, you know exactly how long it takes to get from one place to another on various methods, and can plan your day down to the millisecond with perfect precision. No moment is wasted, and nothing is left to chance. Combined with Entropy 1, this becomes insane! You basically become Batman levels of prepared.<br /> <br /> Mixed with other spheres, you can make on going effects stop at precisely the time you intend them to, no more &quot;stop at the end of a scene, or the day&quot; now it's &quot;Stop precisely at 3pm tomorrow&quot; or &quot;Stop after exactly 15 hours&quot;. You can make Corr. gates which change location at specific times of day, Force bound temperatures that fluctuate between hot and cold depending on whether it's day or night, Spirit gates which only open for one hour at midnight. Guns that morph into gloves during the day... Any effect that you want to have multiple steps to it based on time delays needs Time 1 to pull of. Plus, with Time 1 you can sense all the temporal elements of other mage's effects. So if you come across these Time sensitive gates or items, you may not know what will happen, but you'll certainly know when it will.<br /> <br /> Also, what is the one sphere that when used, no matter how well you've planned, how much you've achieved, how many things you've accomplished, all of that can be rendered moot simply by making it all not happen? Time! What's the one point sphere that actually clues you in to when this kind of stuff is happening? Time 1! Think about it. You're in a battle and everything you throw at them, they seem to be ready for it. Any ambush, any surprise, any secret, they can react to it without a moment's hesitation. The truth is that they're using Time magic to change things to happen their way, and there is no way you could possibly know about this without Time 1. Knowing that mages are messing around with the time stream is impossible without this sphere. You don't know people are spying on you from across time, that they keep undoing your work and sabotaging your attempts before you even get a chance to pull them out of the bag. Time 1 is the only thing that might clue you in to what's going on. Without that, you're pretty much sunk.<br /> <br /> Regarding Time 2, Future and Past sight can be really easily abused if you give the player a chance. They can use it to know almost everything about anything. They know exactly who committed what crimes, where things might have been stolen, where things were hidden, and what people might do if you let them do it. If this sphere was at the 1st rank, it would be even more ridiculous than it already is.<br /> <br /> Besides, Time 2 Future Sight is not exactly unlike Corr. 2 Scrying. Only one is temporal while the other is spatial, so it does make sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>My one iconic roleplay character was a neo-noir, paranormal investigator/drug addict with Time and Spirit Magick, and working towards saving for Prime.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2456-zeroninja","name":"zeroninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}